BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-198805@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260822T100000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T111500
SUMMARY:Kid's Clubhouse: Make Way for Elephants | Session I
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Waitlist On
 ly\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/198805\n\nCelebrate
  the arrival of The Great Elephant Migration in Boston with a hands-on fam
 ily crafting experience inspired by one of the world's most meaningful pub
 lic art initiatives.\n\nLed by children's book author Wendy Rouillard of B
 arnaby's Books & Toys\, young creators will build their own elephant habit
 ats using a variety of nature-inspired materials. Each session begins with
  a brief introduction to the story behind The Great Elephant Migration\,in
 troducing children to the importance of wildlife conservation and the ways
  humans and animals can coexist.\n\nAfter crafting\, continue the adventur
 e with brunch at Café Q\, where families can enjoy Journey to Kerala - a 
 refreshing\, kid-friendly mocktail inspired by the elephants' homeland\, f
 eaturing coconut water\, mango\, ginger\, lime\, curry leaves\, and sparkl
 ing club soda.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members\, 
 plus their children aged 6+. Children may remain in the 'House\, attended 
 by a parent until 4:00PM. Please ensure you select the correct number of c
 hildren's tickets when registering\, so we may account for supplies. Adult
 s do not require registration. If you have a larger family (3+ kids) pleas
 e email happening@thequin.com should you need an additional seat. As we an
 ticipate a waitlist\, please be mindful of other families by making any ne
 cessary cancellations at least 48-hours in advance.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/198805
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
