SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "Damaged Goods" With Paul Scheufele
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 5 spots left\nSt
 atus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/199493
 \n\nThis September\, join us for a thoughtful discussion on Damaged Goods\
 , a compelling work of literary fiction that explores family\, loss\, and 
 the unexpected ways grief can reshape our lives. When Brendan O'Shay inher
 its custody of his late sister's frozen eggs\, he and his family are force
 d to confront difficult questions about love\, legacy\, and what it truly 
 means to honor someone's memory.\n\nSet against the backdrop of the 2008 f
 inancial crisis in New England\, Damaged Goods is an emotionally resonant 
 novel that examines the delicate balance between ambition and compassion. 
 Rich with moral complexity and unforgettable characters\, it is an ideal c
 hoice for readers who enjoy thought-provoking stories that spark meaningfu
 l conversation.\n\nJoined by the author himself\, Paul Scheufele\, and in 
 conversation with Wendy Dodson\, owner of Hummingbird Book\, the evening w
 ill explore the novel’s inspirations\, themes\, and enduring questions. 
 Members will have the opportunity to engage directly with the author in an
  intimate conversation that brings the story vividly to life.\n\n*This eve
 nt is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bit
 es and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations 
 be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/199493
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
